pg:Q10_O0 a ld:AnswerOption ;
    rdfs:label "Ancestor fee rate mining means that a miner looks at each transaction together with all of its unconfirmed ancestors, evaluates them as one package and can take them into the block as one unit; the book says that Core has done ..."@en .

pg:Q10_O2 a ld:AnswerOption ;
    rdfs:label "A lock time is a field of the transaction that says in which block height or at which time the transaction becomes valid."@en .

pg:Q10_O3 a ld:AnswerOption ;
    rdfs:label "The book says in its section on fee sniping that the attack is not very lucrative today because the block subsidy is much higher than the total fees per block, and that at some point in the future fees will be the majority of ..."@en .

